  "mechanism": "Rooted SQL allocates an explicitly disposable workspace without child/parent creation syncs. Scratch may disappear after a crash and supplies no image, publication or recovery authority. All bytes needed for success still require independently durable images and the original committed Raft/required S3 proof. The original durable workspace factory remains unchanged. Both factories share original admission, node locking, full physical retention, bounded removal, synced deletion and quarantine-before-refund behavior.",
  "contracts_preserved": [
    "Original logical identities, captured input, callbacks and uncertain-outcome rules; no retry under a fresh mutation identity.",
    "Original node/group/SQL/image/workspace byte and slot limits, worker counts, operation deadlines, proof checks and owner joins.",
    "Durable create_workspace completes child and parent creation syncs; create_disposable_workspace promises no creation persistence.",
    "Every SQLite/VFS file and private lock retains the complete workspace reservation and exclusive inventory lock.",
    "Last physical release removes the workspace and syncs its parent before refund. Failed/uncertain removal or sync quarantines mutation and retains the whole charge until exclusive reopen recovery.",
    "Reopen discards bounded leftover private files before admission and preserves immutable inventory. No persistent format or marker changes.",
    "Materialized private paths retain their original creation barriers; the new API is selected only by rooted private SQL."
  ],
